/*
 * promo.c - the "promo" GameCube intro rendered with GX (see promo.h)
 *
 * Everything is drawn in the 640x480 pixel space of the reference clip (the logo is
 * an orthographic isometric view).  All timings and colours come from anim_data.h,
 * generated by tools/anim.py, which tools/preview.py also renders on the PC.
 *
 * Frame:
 *   1. logo layer(s): the IPL logo model + "NINTENDO" letters + "GAMECUBE" logotype,
 *      in the glass and/or solid look            -> layer textures (RGBA8, 640x480)
 *   2. composite: layer copies (the "slam" draws several, shifted/stretched)
 *      + light streaks, glints and the cube outline         -> scene texture
 *   3. glow: thresholded, blurred at 1/2 and 1/4 resolution  -> two glow textures
 *   4. output: scene + tinted glow, global fade              -> XFB
 *
 * Rendered exactly as GC-anim-Wii (video.c): the IPL's video modes (592 pixels wide, 448 or
 * 520 lines), its view units and its anti-aliased two-pass frames (each full-frame pass is drawn
 * as a top and a bottom half).  The glow passes alone use a non-AA 24-bit EFB.
 */
